00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:34.640
The R Tesla Motors thread connects model size growth to grid limitations.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:39.940
A Florida homeowner received a $59,000 quote for a solar installation.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:44.820
Commenters attributed part of the high cost to Tesla's pricing and service model.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:49.940
The discussion shows how Tesla's approach influences broader solar quotes in the region.

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:54.660
multiple users pointed to Tesla's component and labor rates as a benchmark.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:06:00.380
The thread reveals how one company's pricing can shape expectations across local installers.

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:06.200
Energy availability sets the practical limit on AI scaling long before chip counts or

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:10.940
algorithm tweaks become the bottleneck. When power delivery itself requires new

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:16.000
substations or dedicated generation, the cost and timeline of each additional watt

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:22.160
shift from a footnote to the central constraint on model size and iteration speed. Tesla's

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:27.240
approach folds energy infrastructure into the same vertical stack that includes custom silicon

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:33.320
and software, which changes the trade-off between speed of deployment and long-term operating cost.

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:39.060
Rivals that rely on third-party power contracts face different risks around rate volatility

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:45.260
and interconnection cues, while Tesla can align generation or storage additions with its own hardware

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:52.040
rollout. This integration also affects megapack and powerwall economics, because excess generation

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:58.260
capacity built for AI can feed back into energy storage products during lower compute demand periods.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:03.380
If energy infrastructure must be built or contracted in parallel with silicon,

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:09.820
the per token cost curve flattens unless utilization stays high enough to amortize the fixed power

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:15.960
assets. That dynamic favors operators who can both generate and consume the electricity inside

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:20.880
a single economic boundary rather than those who treat power as an external input.

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:26.420
The pattern extends beyond training clusters into inference hardware and vehicle platforms.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:32.640
Each new HW5 or AI5 deployment multiplies the energy draw per vehicle,

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:37.820
turning what once looked like a software scaling problem into a distributed power planning

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:44.220
exercise. Before we go, regulatory filings expected in the coming days could clarify timelines

